    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_00f0b7094e0586b3dd3d6eab0c115e309bb1dd2155e2a57e73088866114bbb09",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses the H_P basis theorem twice at different scales. First, periodic/reflection symmetry and an isometric Fourier rescaling identify the E_n as a complete basis of H_P. Then fractional-part folding sends an arbitrary compactly supported function into H_P, expansion in the E_n converts that folded function into the dilation-generated closure of E1, and rescaling returns an explicit approximation in the ambient space H. A cited Mellin-Wiener nonvanishing criterion gives a separate spectral explanation of the same dilation completeness.",
