    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2702b9459f80095fadc57e3c4222f3c93312d47385ad8ee5723048950b423670",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the raw Mobius approximants, the paper turns the unresolved low-coordinate portion of the domination criterion into an exact energy calculation and derives simultaneous smallness requirements on two Mobius partial-sum combinations along any successful subsequence. The following smoothed construction changes mu(q)/q to mu(q)/q^(1+epsilon_n), using positive epsilon_n to control truncated Dirichlet-series tails while epsilon_n tends to zero so the fixed coordinates still approach those of -E1. This is a motivated regularization of the natural scheme, not an unconditional resolution of its low-coordinate obstruction.",
