    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3a76dd391739468e22a5af22d60008d564e77b95baf3fccf364a6072bbef1418",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper converts its RH-linked weighted-Hilbert-space closure target into an arithmetic coefficient problem in stages: the differences e_q lie in the periodic, reflection-antisymmetric subspace H_P; consecutive sine differences form an orthonormal basis of that subspace through an isometric Fourier model; and each e_q has an explicit harmonic-sum coordinate in that basis. Thus approximation of E1 becomes l2 convergence of an arithmetic coefficient array, with uniform square-summable domination as the remaining analytic burden.",
