    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_422ca5faac817be2589af216e2a802a089b946472a3578711ca02bf7f81da79b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The three approximation families share the same coefficient-space strategy but localize its unresolved norm-control burden differently. The triangular family enforces exact cancellation through a growing low-coordinate block and leaves the window n < p <= n^4 after remote-tail control; the raw and exponent-smoothed Mobius families obtain the target limit only for each fixed coordinate and leave 1 <= p <= n^2 log n after their remote-tail estimates. Each resulting RH statement remains conditional on a common square-summable envelope along infinitely many n.",
